WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.493
[BRIEFING WITH THE DIRECTOR]
(The story in this book is already over.)

00:00:43.518 --> 00:00:46.068
(Whatever happened is now over.)

00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:46.724
Okay.

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:50.623
(The first part of the MV will be depressing, ...)

00:00:50.648 --> 00:00:52.787
(because you can’t find this lost page.)

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.200
(The more you look for it, …)

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.280
(the more confused you become.)

00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:16.978
Hello, everyone!

00:01:17.003 --> 00:01:21.640
Today we’re shooting the MV of my own song

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.013
“GLITCH”.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.186
It’s also a soundtrack for the series

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.240
“MOONSHADOW”.

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:30.845
Here’s the story.

00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:38.806
I’m looking for some lost memories in a book.

00:01:39.087 --> 00:01:41.000
As I go through the pages,

00:01:41.025 --> 00:01:42.294
I come across so many memories.

00:01:42.319 --> 00:01:44.600
Though the last page is missing.

00:01:44.802 --> 00:01:48.080
So I look for it everywhere, but to no avail.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.041
BONNIE tags along with me,

00:01:50.628 --> 00:01:52.240
but we still can’t find it.

00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:55.560
And that’s how the story concludes.

00:01:55.627 --> 00:01:57.840
If it’s not meant to be found,
it won’t be found.

00:01:57.978 --> 00:02:00.810
It tells us to just let it go, to move on!!!

00:02:00.842 --> 00:02:03.873
To enjoy the present.

00:02:03.896 --> 00:02:06.229
It’s fine not to find what is lost.

00:02:06.337 --> 00:02:11.480
You can still find good memories along the way
that you can cherish.

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:12.695
It’s something like that.

00:02:12.773 --> 00:02:14.084
It’s not only about exes.

00:02:14.109 --> 00:02:15.995
It can be about many more things,
depending on your interpretation.

00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:17.253
Take your time with it.

00:02:17.287 --> 00:02:18.960
Set it on repeat.

00:02:19.032 --> 00:02:22.280
The MV has a bluish-gray color scheme,

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.960
With a slight touch of melancholy,

00:02:24.044 --> 00:02:32.234
and a sense of playful elegance.

00:02:32.787 --> 00:02:34.400
It’s not that sad, though.

00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:35.868
Keep listening to it and you’ll find out.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.654
Give it some views for me.

00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:41.080
I think I love this song,

00:02:41.286 --> 00:02:44.127
and I rarely get to sing songs in this tone.

00:02:44.152 --> 00:02:46.621
Normally I sing love songs and the like,

00:02:46.646 --> 00:02:48.760
but this one is a bit sad.

00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:51.965
It also has notes I’ve never sung before,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.057
and the recording took so long.

00:02:54.144 --> 00:02:56.535
There’re lots of details in the song,

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.454
so I want everyone to give it a shot.

00:02:58.737 --> 00:03:01.019
The song and the series link up perfectly.

00:03:01.044 --> 00:03:04.400
Every time the song plays over a scene,

00:03:04.463 --> 00:03:07.240
it really adds depth to your feelings.

00:03:08.622 --> 00:03:10.152
Let’s see how it’ll be like today.

00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:11.560
We’ve only just begun.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.480
We’ll spend the whole day looking for the last page.

00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:14.840
In the end, we wouldn’t find it.

00:03:15.017 --> 00:03:15.721
But that’s fine.

00:03:15.746 --> 00:03:17.520
Tell me if you’ve found the last page for me,

00:03:17.545 --> 00:03:18.892
but I don’t need it anyway.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.960
[EMI’S MV GIRL ENTERS THE SCENE]

00:03:49.153 --> 00:03:50.640
Hello!

00:03:50.838 --> 00:03:53.791
While waiting for P’MI to find the last page,

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.696
I’m taking a moral support nap for her.

00:03:56.805 --> 00:03:58.520
(Will you help her find the last page today?)

00:03:58.558 --> 00:04:01.760
Nope. She has to find it herself.

00:04:01.878 --> 00:04:04.280
My only job is to support her.

00:04:04.685 --> 00:04:07.400
(P’MI said she’s after the book’s last page.)

00:04:07.468 --> 00:04:08.150
Oh!

00:04:08.175 --> 00:04:10.080
Then she’s still dwelling in the story!!!

00:04:10.871 --> 00:04:12.480
She doesn’t want it to end yet.

00:04:12.541 --> 00:04:13.805
It means she hasn’t moved on!!

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.400
(She said it has nothing to do with her ex.)

00:04:15.662 --> 00:04:16.800
It certainly does.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.400
From the story I heard, it does.

00:04:19.598 --> 00:04:21.080
The book has only old memories

00:04:21.105 --> 00:04:22.160
and no ending.

00:04:22.185 --> 00:04:23.920
Basically, she moved on in a circle.

00:04:24.126 --> 00:04:27.160
That’s why she needs the last page,
to finally have a fresh start.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.880
It’s 100% a story about an ex.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:29.835
Definitely.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.280
(Can you two write a new ending together?)

00:04:32.319 --> 00:04:33.225
I don’t know.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.344
She has to move on and reach out herself.

00:04:35.369 --> 00:04:36.560
The ending is just that.

00:04:36.593 --> 00:04:38.913
The old story is already over,
and now it’s time to start a new one.

00:04:38.938 --> 00:04:40.280
(Do you want to?)

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.800
I’m that new book waiting for her to pick up!!!

00:04:42.879 --> 00:04:44.231
I’m not that lost page.

00:04:44.253 --> 00:04:46.089
I’m the new one waiting for her.

00:04:46.122 --> 00:04:47.800
But she’s still picking up the old one.

00:04:47.974 --> 00:04:49.120
What does that mean?

00:04:49.145 --> 00:04:51.880
She wants to go to old,
familiar places with a new partner?

00:04:52.335 --> 00:04:53.840
What does that even mean?

00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:55.695
A new book has to tell a new story.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.773
How could it tell an old story

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.932
while including a new partner?
[HOW COULD SHE DO IT?!!]

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.400
It means P’CHAN wrote this song
with her ex in mind.

00:05:00.539 --> 00:05:01.360
I can’t wait to hear

00:05:01.385 --> 00:05:02.689
what she has to say about this.
[NOW WE NEED TO TALK!!]

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.875
The previous song is also one

00:05:04.988 --> 00:05:06.514
that the protagonist writes for their partner,

00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:09.151
hoping to win their love

00:05:09.219 --> 00:05:10.640
and make them forget their ex.

00:05:10.753 --> 00:05:12.778
But this song is especially written for the ex.

00:05:12.803 --> 00:05:13.746
[STILL ABOUT HER EX!!]

00:05:13.771 --> 00:05:16.575
That’s great. Just great.

00:05:17.258 --> 00:05:19.160
It’s like the relationship between KEY, CHAN,
and JAY.

00:05:20.164 --> 00:05:21.920
(We’ll be asking her about this the entire day.)

00:05:22.249 --> 00:05:23.805
Okay. We’ll go ask her over there.

00:05:24.215 --> 00:05:25.000
Haha.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.260
Ask her.

00:05:26.433 --> 00:05:27.760
[DID SOMEONE JUST CALL ME?]

00:05:27.785 --> 00:05:29.720
Look into her innocent, twinkling eyes.

00:05:29.771 --> 00:05:32.000
What? What happened?

00:05:32.025 --> 00:05:33.000
She doesn’t even know.

00:05:33.025 --> 00:05:35.760
(She said you wrote this song for your ex.)

00:05:36.256 --> 00:05:37.280
That’s not true!

00:05:37.523 --> 00:05:38.600
I’m not the writer!!

00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:43.360
Actually, when I listen to it, I feel
it tells the stories of both KEY and CHAN.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.454
But it’s CHAN’s song.

00:05:44.554 --> 00:05:49.480
True, but I feel N’KEY’s longing for P’CHAN
through the words, something like that.

00:05:49.589 --> 00:05:51.520
And nothing about CHAN’s longing for KEY?

00:05:51.615 --> 00:05:52.553
It’s either ‘KEY misses CHAN’

00:05:52.578 --> 00:05:54.258
-or ‘CHAN misses JAY’.
-It’s a sad song, after all.

00:05:54.478 --> 00:05:56.546
It conveys a sense of wistful longing.
[WISTFUL LONGING]

00:05:56.616 --> 00:05:57.960
(It’s open to interpretation.)

00:05:57.981 --> 00:05:58.640
That’s right.

00:05:58.694 --> 00:06:01.697
[OPEN TO INTERPRETATION]
The message is entirely up to viewers’
interpretations.

00:06:01.784 --> 00:06:05.844
The song is often used in flashback scenes.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.080
(Did I get away with it?)

00:06:08.212 --> 00:06:09.212
(Yeah!)

00:06:10.298 --> 00:06:11.280
(Come closer.)

00:06:22.196 --> 00:06:24.375
(Okay, cut! That would do.)

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.711
(How many books have you read today?)

00:06:25.804 --> 00:06:28.960
Just one. The one I can never finish.

00:06:29.008 --> 00:06:31.396
I read it again and again! Haha.

00:06:31.436 --> 00:06:32.646
(Have you found a satisfying answer?)

00:06:32.705 --> 00:06:34.000
No, not yet.

00:06:34.036 --> 00:06:36.307
I was just looking for the lost page,

00:06:36.337 --> 00:06:38.042
but still couldn’t find it.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.662
I was stuck on the same old book.

00:06:39.797 --> 00:06:41.036
I may have a thing for it.

00:06:41.602 --> 00:06:42.952
What does that mean?

00:06:42.977 --> 00:06:45.440
She wants to go to old,
familiar places with a new partner?

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:46.960
What does that even mean?

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.880
(Steals a glance at EMI)

00:07:04.715 --> 00:07:06.440
[SHE’S SECRETLY SMILING!!]

00:07:13.257 --> 00:07:14.760
[A SAD SONG (?)]

00:07:18.194 --> 00:07:22.840
Yeah! We finally finished shooting for today.

00:07:22.928 --> 00:07:28.600
Yes! It’s my own song, “GLITCH”.

00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:36.400
I hope everyone enjoy it, and if you do,
please give it a Like.

00:07:36.425 --> 00:07:39.095
If you don’t, you can give me
a moral support Like first

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.520
and criticize it later.

00:07:40.557 --> 00:07:42.677
Anyway, please give me a Like.

00:07:42.939 --> 00:07:43.901
Where can I listen to it, P’MI?

00:07:43.926 --> 00:07:45.991
-I’m dying for it now!
-Oh! It’s available on

00:07:46.016 --> 00:07:48.196
YouTube: RISER MUSIC

00:07:48.221 --> 00:07:51.680
and all other streaming platforms.

00:07:52.162 --> 00:07:53.520
(How do you feel to have BONNIE)

00:07:53.545 --> 00:07:54.360
(as the MV girl?)

00:07:54.385 --> 00:07:56.225
I’m delighted!

00:07:56.272 --> 00:07:57.396
I think it’s unexpected for her!!!

00:07:58.659 --> 00:08:00.560
But for whom did she write this song again?

00:08:00.618 --> 00:08:02.532
Yeah, for whom?

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:03.610
(I have nothing to do with it, right?)

00:08:03.635 --> 00:08:05.758
-I have nothing to do with it. I’m not the writer.
-But you’re the singer!

00:08:05.981 --> 00:08:07.542
Well, yes! I’m just the singer!

00:08:07.572 --> 00:08:08.415
And who’s the MV girl?

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:08.979
Tell them.

00:08:09.025 --> 00:08:11.885
-My true leading lady…
-Tell your side chick.

00:08:11.919 --> 00:08:13.103
-Who? Haha.
-Your side chick.

00:08:13.751 --> 00:08:16.434
My leading lady is only you!

00:08:16.459 --> 00:08:17.461
Understood, everyone?

00:08:17.486 --> 00:08:18.380
Yeah, that’s it.

00:08:18.405 --> 00:08:19.788
That just breaks your heart, right?

00:08:19.813 --> 00:08:20.746
Haha.

00:08:20.774 --> 00:08:22.120
You’re all heartbroken now.

00:08:22.143 --> 00:08:23.210
Anyway, please give me a Like

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:24.059
-whether you enjoy it or not.
-Leave a comment and create a hashtag

00:08:24.092 --> 00:08:24.854
#banBONNIE.

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:25.643
Haha.
[DOESN’T SOUND GOOD!!]

00:08:25.668 --> 00:08:26.600
(Now you’re being mean. I’ll cut this part out.)

00:08:26.625 --> 00:08:27.516
Stop! Cut it out.

00:08:54.023 --> 00:08:57.720
Help! I’m being grounded!
[THEY HAVEN’T LET YOU LEAVE YET!!]

00:08:58.294 --> 00:08:59.364
(Do you find the acting hard?)

00:08:59.389 --> 00:09:01.511
It’s not, but I’m tired now.

00:09:01.643 --> 00:09:02.640
(Haha.)

00:09:04.381 --> 00:09:05.480
(Hang in there.)

00:09:05.663 --> 00:09:06.850
(Yawn)

00:09:07.903 --> 00:09:09.311
(Do you have a way to handle tiredness?)

00:09:09.336 --> 00:09:10.016
I go to sleep.

00:09:10.056 --> 00:09:10.760
(Haha.)

00:09:11.512 --> 00:09:12.520
(She’s not wrong!!)

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.320
(Just a bit more, and you can go home.)

00:09:15.414 --> 00:09:16.200
You’re kidding me.

00:09:16.644 --> 00:09:18.600
I just got told to do more scenes.

00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:19.600
Help me please.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.560
They won’t let me leave.

00:09:22.711 --> 00:09:24.600
If you don’t use the scenes in the end,
It’ll piss me off!!!

00:09:24.625 --> 00:09:25.360
What’s going on?

00:09:25.408 --> 00:09:28.637
(She said, if we added her to your line sync
scene only to cut her out in the end,

00:09:28.662 --> 00:09:29.480
she’d get angry.)

00:09:29.553 --> 00:09:30.680
If you cut me off…

00:09:31.862 --> 00:09:36.000
If P’MI looks at it, thinks ‘I look weird in this’,
and then cuts it off, I’ll be so mad.

00:10:18.828 --> 00:10:22.438
♪ My whole heart still keeps on missing you like this ♪

00:10:22.934 --> 00:10:27.913
♪ You’re like a love song that I can’t forget ♪

00:10:28.276 --> 00:10:32.680
♪ I still hear your voice every minute ♪

00:10:32.944 --> 00:10:35.613
♪ Your image never fades ♪

00:10:35.948 --> 00:10:39.960
♪ No matter how I try to erase it ♪

00:10:40.332 --> 00:10:44.086
♪ 'Cause my heart still keeps on missing you like this ♪

00:10:44.286 --> 00:10:49.200
♪ You’re like a love song that I can’t forget ♪

00:10:49.562 --> 00:10:56.835
♪ Every melody plays on a loop, never fades ♪

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.560
(The rest are all EMI’s solo scenes.)

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.860
[BONNIE WRAPPED]
Wow!

00:11:00.885 --> 00:11:02.080
(You can finally go home.)

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.240
I’m leaving now.
[LET’S GO HOME]

00:11:04.374 --> 00:11:08.270
-(Do you have anything to say to EMI?)
-I leave the rest to P’MI because it’s her song.

00:11:08.295 --> 00:11:09.608
Of course. Rest assured.

00:11:09.641 --> 00:11:11.233
The MV girl has finished her duty here.

00:11:11.258 --> 00:11:15.388
I hope you guessed right about
who P’MI's MV girl would be.

00:11:15.638 --> 00:11:17.240
Actually, we haven’t taken a shot of your face.

00:11:17.265 --> 00:11:18.800
-We recorded, like, only your figure.
-Oh!

00:11:18.837 --> 00:11:19.654
[VISIBLY UPSET]
Then what’s the point of all the makeup?

00:11:20.607 --> 00:11:21.281
Am I pretty?

00:11:21.306 --> 00:11:23.013
(Yes! Come behind the cam and take a look.)

00:11:23.057 --> 00:11:24.560
Am I pretty? I am, right?

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:29.520
In the line sync scene we just did,
BONNIE also showed up from time to time.

00:11:29.693 --> 00:11:32.720
At first, I thought the line sync scene should
include her,

00:11:32.745 --> 00:11:33.949
 otherwise it would’ve been me
singing alone, which would be so lonely.

00:11:33.974 --> 00:11:34.873
[LONELY WITHOUT YOU]

00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:36.205
Are line sync scenes usually solo?

00:11:36.543 --> 00:11:37.520
They are?!
[THE SCENES ARE SOLO?]

00:11:37.758 --> 00:11:39.520
But we’re a duo!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.680
We’re inseparable!

00:11:40.752 --> 00:11:43.480
I feel we’ve been quite productive today.

00:11:43.672 --> 00:11:44.127
(Yeah.)

00:11:44.156 --> 00:11:45.889
Everything went just fine.

00:11:46.261 --> 00:11:47.240
But I’m rather tired now.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.283
-Oh, right, I just had a meal.
-(You also worked late last night.)

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.696
Did I work late last night?

00:11:50.752 --> 00:11:51.939
But, hey, I’m still up for hire.

00:11:51.964 --> 00:11:53.484
[STILL UP FOR HIRE]
I still want to work, work, work.

00:11:53.772 --> 00:11:56.375
Don’t worry, everyone. I may look tired now,

00:11:56.392 --> 00:11:58.560
but once on set, I’ll look just as lively as ever.
[WORK REFRESHES ME]

00:11:58.773 --> 00:11:59.800
(Show us how lively you are on set.)

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.258
[REFRESHED IN THE BLINK OF AN EYE]

00:12:02.579 --> 00:12:03.520
(You nailed it.)

00:12:04.166 --> 00:12:05.040
Today I look a bit too soft and sweet.

00:12:05.293 --> 00:12:06.328
I should look a bit sadder.

00:12:06.353 --> 00:12:07.353
(Sadder.)

00:12:07.701 --> 00:12:09.400
Anyway, please enjoy the song,

00:12:09.425 --> 00:12:11.240
which is one of many that I love.
[I JUST LVOE IT]

00:12:11.445 --> 00:12:13.000
I’ve found the last page,

00:12:13.572 --> 00:12:15.960
after an angel handed it to me.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.030
(Wow!)

00:12:17.208 --> 00:12:18.520
An angel on Earth.
[ANGEL BONNIE ON EARTH]

00:12:19.224 --> 00:12:21.640
She gave me the last page of this book.

00:12:22.059 --> 00:12:23.482
(It took you so long to find it.)

00:12:23.507 --> 00:12:25.040
It took me the entire song to find it.
[TOOK HER THE ENTIRE SONG!!]

00:12:25.358 --> 00:12:28.560
But then I realized the page meant nothing

00:12:28.589 --> 00:12:30.480
as it belonged to the old book. So I closed it.

00:12:31.258 --> 00:12:32.560
The new one was right in front of me.
[SHE WENT FOR THE NEW ONE]

00:12:33.726 --> 00:12:36.400
I took her hand and asked her out on a date.

00:12:59.088 --> 00:13:01.818
It’s now officially finished,
[SHOOTING FINISHED]

00:13:01.843 --> 00:13:05.658
the shooting of the MV for my song “GLITCH”.

00:13:05.708 --> 00:13:10.079
Please enjoy it, everyone, and don’t you dare
forget about it.

00:13:10.267 --> 00:13:11.640
Now, repeat after me 3 times.

00:13:11.665 --> 00:13:12.920
GLITCH x1

00:13:12.981 --> 00:13:13.981
GLITCH x2

00:13:14.023 --> 00:13:15.495
GLITCH x3

00:13:16.559 --> 00:13:17.240
Please give it a shot.

00:13:17.265 --> 00:13:21.179
The set today is just stunning, so the MV
should turn out fine.

00:13:21.215 --> 00:13:23.771
Today I’m here with my same old MV girl.
[MY ONE AND ONLY MV GIRL!]

00:13:23.796 --> 00:13:24.680
I’ve never changed MV girl.

00:13:24.705 --> 00:13:26.400
There’s always only her for me.

00:13:26.525 --> 00:13:27.374
(And where is she now?)

00:13:27.421 --> 00:13:30.644
She left already after her final scene.
[ALREADY BACK HOME TO REST]

00:13:30.674 --> 00:13:33.367
It’s my song, so I had to stay a bit longer.

00:13:33.688 --> 00:13:36.690
You can enjoy this song, GLITCH—

00:13:36.715 --> 00:13:37.880
I said it again—
